  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "An array AAA of length NNN is said to be good if A1⋅A2⋅…AN=A1+A2+…+ANA_1 \\cdot A_2 \\cdot \\ldots A_N = A_1 + A_2 + \\ldots + A_NA1​⋅A2​⋅…AN​=A1​+A2​+…+AN​, i.e. product equals sum.\n\nGiven an array AAA of length NNN, count how many subarrays of AAA are good. Formally, find the number of pairs (L,R)(L, R)(L,R) such that:\n\n\n1≤L≤R≤N1 \\le L \\le R \\le N1≤L≤R≤N\nThe array [AL,AL+1,AL+2,…,AR][A_L, A_{L + 1}, A_{L + 2}, \\ldots, A_R][AL​,AL+1​,AL+2​,…,AR​] is good.\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains NNN - the size of the array.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the number of good subarrays of AAA.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Ai≤N1 \\le A_i \\le N1≤Ai​≤N",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n3\n2 1 3\n4\n2 2 2 2\n6\n1 2 1 4 1 1\n1\n1",
        "output": "4\n7\n8\n1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 1 : The good subarrays are [2],[1],[3][2], [1], [3][2],[1],[3] and [2,1,3][2, 1, 3][2,1,3].\nTest Case 2 : [2][2][2] and [2,2][2, 2][2,2] are good. [2][2][2] occurs 444 times, and [2,2][2, 2][2,2] occurs 333 times."
      }
    ]
  },
